! TDDFT mode matrix 10/16 -- state dipoles, GMH analysis, MOLDEN export
!
! HeH+ / STO-3G, the smallest charge-transfer-like system.  Exercises
! three things no other case touches:
!   %tddft_dipmom  -- unrelaxed excited-state dipoles, transition
!                     dipoles, and the Cave-Newton GMH coupling;
!   %export_tddft  -- *_tddft_mo.molden and *_tddft_states.txt writers;
!   a CHARGED system -- state dipoles are origin-dependent for ions,
!                     which the output header must state.
!
! Numerically anchored independently in tests/test_v0871_heh_tddft_dip.inp
! (hand-coded python RHF+CIS reference); here the point is that the
! export files are produced and the analysis block runs.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     energy
%charge  1
%mult    1
%tddft   1
%tddft_tda on
%tddft_dipmom on
%export_tddft on
%geom angstrom
He  0.0  0.0  0.0
H   0.0  0.0  0.793765816355
*end
